In industry, sulphur dioxide can be prepared by roasting zinc sulphide and $iron pyrites.
\begin{aligned}
& 2 \mathrm{ZnS}_{(\mathrm{s})}+3 \mathrm{O}_{2(\mathrm{ g})} \stackrel{\Delta}{\longrightarrow} 2 \mathrm{ZnO}_{(\mathrm{s})}+2 \mathrm{SO}_{2(\mathrm{ g})} \\
& 4 \mathrm{FeS}_{2(\mathrm{ s})}+11 \mathrm{O}_{2(\mathrm{ g})} \stackrel{\Delta}{\longrightarrow} 2 \mathrm{Fe}_2 \mathrm{O}_{3(\mathrm{ s})}+8 \mathrm{SO}_{2(\mathrm{ g})}
\end{aligned}$
